@page
@model IndexModel
@{
    ViewData["Title"] = "Home";
}

<section class="hero-section">
    <h1>IT support that doesn't live in a group chat.</h1>
    <p class="lede">
        HelpDeskTicketing gives small teams and growing organizations a
        simple way to log, track, and resolve tech issues — without buying
        into a full enterprise service desk.
    </p>

    @if (User.Identity?.IsAuthenticated != true)
    {
        <div class="hero-actions">
            <a asp-area="Identity" asp-page="/Account/Register" class="btn btn-primary btn-lg">Get Started</a>
            <a asp-area="Identity" asp-page="/Account/Login" class="btn btn-outline-primary btn-lg">Sign In</a>
        </div>
    }
    else if (User.IsInRole("ITAgent") || User.IsInRole("Admin"))
    {
        <div class="hero-actions">
            <a asp-page="/Dashboard" class="btn btn-primary btn-lg">View Dashboard</a>
            <a asp-page="/Agent/AllTickets" class="btn btn-outline-primary btn-lg">All Tickets</a>
        </div>
    }
    else
    {
        <div class="hero-actions">
            <a asp-page="/Tickets/Create" class="btn btn-primary btn-lg">Submit a Ticket</a>
            <a asp-page="/Tickets/MyTickets" class="btn btn-outline-primary btn-lg">My Tickets</a>
        </div>
    }
</section>

<section class="steps-section">
    <div class="step">
        <span class="step-num">1</span>
        <h3>Log the issue</h3>
        <p>Anyone on the team can submit a ticket in under a minute — no more digging through chat history to find who reported what.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="step">
        <span class="step-num">2</span>
        <h3>Get it assigned</h3>
        <p>An agent picks it up, so there's always a clear owner instead of a message everyone assumes someone else will handle.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="step">
        <span class="step-num">3</span>
        <h3>Track it to resolution</h3>
        <p>Status updates and comments stay attached to the ticket, so nothing gets lost when people move on to the next thing.</p>
    </div>
</section>

<section class="why-section">
    <h2>Why this exists</h2>
    <p>
        Most small teams don't have a dedicated IT department — so tech
        issues get handled the same way everything else does: a message
        in the group chat, a quick "hey can you look at this," and no real
        record of what happened. That works fine until it doesn't — until
        three people report the same printer issue separately, or a fix
        gets forgotten because it scrolled out of view. HelpDeskTicketing
        is a small, focused tool built to fix exactly that gap.
    </p>
</section>